\section{The block}{

Each function receives \code{blk}, the block: a list with \code{dim} (the
number of coefficients per level), \code{n_levels}, \code{levels}, \code{cnms} (the
coefficient names), \code{theta_idx} and \code{b_idx}, and for a field \code{aux},
the fixed data \code{term$build} returned. \code{b} is level-major: the \code{dim}
coefficients of one level are contiguous, so \code{matrix(b, nrow = dim)}
has one level per column. Read the block with \code{[[}, never \code{$}; see
\code{\link[=frm_hazard_reads]{frm_hazard_reads()}}.

\code{lpdf} runs on the TAPE: \code{b} and \code{theta} are RTMB advectors there.
Use \code{RTMB::matrix()} and \code{RTMB::dmvnorm()} or \code{RTMB::dgmrf()}, and
write the density without loops over levels. The other functions run
on numbers.
}

\section{A field term}{

\code{term} is a list:
\describe{
\item{\code{args}}{The special's argument names in positional order. It
must include \code{"gr"}, the grouping variable. frmtmb matches a call
against them by position and by exact name, and refuses an
unknown or misspelled argument.}
\item{\code{parse}}{\verb{function(args, env)}: \code{args} is the named list of
unevaluated argument expressions (\code{NULL} for an absent one), and
\code{env} the formula environment. Check the arguments and return a
list, the spec, which \code{build} receives. Do not evaluate data
here; the data are not known yet.}
\item{\code{build}}{\verb{function(spec, gr, lookup)}: \code{gr} holds the grouping
values of the rows, and \code{lookup(expr, what)} resolves an argument
expression from \code{data2}, the data and the formula environment,
as \code{gr(cov = A)} resolves its matrix. Return
\code{list(levels, index, aux)}: \code{levels} the block's level labels,
\code{index} the level of each row (whole numbers into \code{levels}), and
\code{aux} the fixed data the other functions read as \code{blk[["aux"]]}.
Add \code{expands = TRUE} when the block's coefficients are a fixed
linear map of its parameters (see \code{expand}).}
\item{\code{usage}}{How the special is written, for messages:
\code{"car(M, gr = g)"}.}
\item{\code{levels_of}}{Optional. \verb{function(gr)} giving the level labels
of grouping values, when they are not \code{as.character(gr)}. It is
used on new data too.}
\item{\code{levels_complete}}{Optional. \code{TRUE} when \code{levels} is the whole
index set of the structure (every mesh node), so a value outside
it is not an unseen level.}
}
