\section{Rows a field reports}{

A field's theta is usually not a set of brms \verb{sd_<group>__<coef>}
and \code{cor_} parameters. Give \code{natural} for such a structure:
\verb{function(theta, blk)} returning \code{list(term, type, est, grad)}, one
entry per reported row. \code{type} is \code{"sd"} or \code{"range"} (estimated on
the log scale), \code{"prop"} (logit), \code{"cor"} (Fisher z) or \code{"raw"};
\code{est} is the value on that scale and \code{grad} its jacobian in \code{theta},
a matrix with one row per term. \code{\link[=confint_varcorr]{confint_varcorr()}} reports the rows
with delta-method intervals. A structure with \code{natural} is a field
for brms's names too: \code{\link[=ngrps]{ngrps()}}, \code{\link[=VarCorr]{VarCorr()}} and \code{\link[=variables]{variables()}} do not
count it as a grouping factor.
}

\section{Testing a structure}{

Compare the fitted log-likelihood with one you compute independently:
for a gaussian response, integrate the block out by hand and evaluate
the marginal density with \code{mvtnorm::dmvnorm()} or a dense
\code{solve()}. A test that registers calls \code{\link[=frmtmb_local_registries]{frmtmb_local_registries()}}
first, which restores every registry when the test ends.
}

\examples{
# an exchangeable block with a FIXED correlation of 0.5 and one
# estimated standard deviation: xcs(0 + t | g)
xcs_lpdf <- function(b, theta, blk) {
  d <- blk[["dim"]]
  C <- RTMB::matrix(0.5, d, d) + diag(0.5, d)
  Sigma <- exp(2 * theta[1]) * C
  dim(b) <- c(d, length(b) \%/\% d)
  sum(RTMB::dmvnorm(t(b), 0, Sigma, log = TRUE))
}
xcs_vcov <- function(theta, blk) {
  d <- blk[["dim"]]
  V <- exp(2 * theta[1]) * (matrix(0.5, d, d) + diag(0.5, d))
  dimnames(V) <- list(blk[["cnms"]], blk[["cnms"]])
  V
}
\dontrun{
# in the contributing package's .onLoad()
frmtmb_register_covstruct("xcs", lpdf = xcs_lpdf, vcov = xcs_vcov,
                          npar = 1L, sd_idx = 1L)
}
}
